      <memberdef kind="function" id="bsp__gpio_8h_1aa6be43410ae12aa3bbb746fb562352cd" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void bspGpioAnalogReadResolution</definition>
        <argsstring>(uint8_t bits)</argsstring>
        <name>bspGpioAnalogReadResolution</name>
        <param>
          <type>uint8_t</type>
          <declname>bits</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function sets the size (in bits) of the value returned by <ref refid="bsp__gpio_8h_1a34347317f123b2222eb416e5e5c56091" kindref="member">bspGpioAnalogRead()</ref>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">bits</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The resolution (in bits). You can set this between 1 and 32.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>If you set the <ref refid="bsp__gpio_8h_1aa6be43410ae12aa3bbb746fb562352cd" kindref="member">bspGpioAnalogReadResolution()</ref> value to a value higher than your board’s capabilities, the board will only report back at its highest resolution, padding the extra bits with zeros.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If you set the <ref refid="bsp__gpio_8h_1aa6be43410ae12aa3bbb746fb562352cd" kindref="member">bspGpioAnalogReadResolution()</ref> value to a value lower than your board’s capabilities, the extra least significant bits read from the ADC will be discarded.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>None </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
