      <memberdef kind="function" id="bsp__gpio_8h_1a473ea43016c7438bcf6c54ae0953b44b" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void bspGpioAnalogWriteResolution</definition>
        <argsstring>(uint8_t bits)</argsstring>
        <name>bspGpioAnalogWriteResolution</name>
        <param>
          <type>uint8_t</type>
          <declname>bits</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function sets the resolution of the <ref refid="bsp__gpio_8h_1a9b2f7d9d0077df86b5fbd73942bcaffc" kindref="member">bspGpioAnalogWrite()</ref> function. It defaults to 8 bits (values between 0-255). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">bits</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The resolution (in bits). The value can range from 1 to 32.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>If you set the <ref refid="bsp__gpio_8h_1a473ea43016c7438bcf6c54ae0953b44b" kindref="member">bspGpioAnalogWriteResolution()</ref> value to a value higher than your board’s capabilities, the board will discard the extra bits.</para>
