      <memberdef kind="function" id="bsp__gpio_8h_1a859d94545c79f456b2914ae7f5a39b70" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void bspGpioNoTone</definition>
        <argsstring>(uint8_t pin)</argsstring>
        <name>bspGpioNoTone</name>
        <param>
          <type>uint8_t</type>
          <declname>pin</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function stops the generation of a square wave triggered by <ref refid="bsp__gpio_8h_1a6b231e4d7b1dd20157b0885b022f9dff" kindref="member">bspGpioTone()</ref>. Has no effect if no tone is being generated. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">pin</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The pin on which to stop generating the tone</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para>If you want to play different pitches on multiple pins, you need to call <ref refid="bsp__gpio_8h_1a859d94545c79f456b2914ae7f5a39b70" kindref="member">bspGpioNoTone()</ref> on one pin before calling <ref refid="bsp__gpio_8h_1a6b231e4d7b1dd20157b0885b022f9dff" kindref="member">bspGpioTone()</ref> on the next pin.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>None </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
